# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(a) You can simply use intuition and symmetry to say $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0$. To show explicitly:\n"
msgstr "(a) Você pode simplesmente usar intuição e simetria para dizer que $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0$. Para mostrar explicitamente:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\langle0|+\\langle1|) Z \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}(\\langle0|Z|0\\rangle+\\langle0|Z|1\\rangle+\\langle1|Z|0\\rangle+\\langle1|Z|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}((1)\\langle0|0\\rangle+(-1)\\langle0|1\\rangle+(1)\\langle1|0\\rangle+(-1)\\langle1|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}(1+0+0+-1)\\\\\n"
"& = 0\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\langle0|+\\langle1|) Z \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}(\\langle0|Z|0\\rangle+\\langle0|Z|1\\rangle+\\langle1|Z|0\\rangle+\\langle1|Z|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}((1)\\langle0|0\\rangle+(-1)\\langle0|1\\rangle+(1)\\langle1|0\\rangle+(-1)\\langle1|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}(1+0+0+-1)\\\\\n"
"& = 0\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(b) The state could collapse to either $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$ when measured, each with 50% chance. But of the 50% that collapse to the $|0\\rangle$ state, 1% of those (or 0.5% of all cases) will be mis-reported as $|1\\rangle$. Of the 50% that collapse to $|1\\rangle$, 10% (or 5% of all cases) will be mis-reported as $|0\\rangle$. This leaves us with:\n"
"* $|0\\rangle$ 54.5%\n"
"* $|1\\rangle$ 45.5%\n"
"Ignoring all other types of possible errors, we would obtain an estimate of\n"
msgstr ""
"(b) O estado pode colapsar para $|0\\rangle$ ou $|1\\rangle$ quando medido, cada um com 50% de chance. Mas, dos 50% que colapsam para o estado $|0\\rangle$, 1% deles (ou 0,5% de todos os casos) serão relatados incorretamente como $|1\\rangle$. Dos 50% que colapsam para $|1\\rangle$, 10% (ou 5% de todos os casos) serão relatados incorretamente como $|0\\rangle$. Isso nos deixa com:\n"
"* $|0\\rangle$ 54,5%\n"
"* $|1\\rangle$ 45,5%\n"
"Ignorando todos os outros tipos de erros possíveis, obteríamos uma estimativa de\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle = (0.545)(1)+(0.455)(-1) = 0.09\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle = (0.545)(1)+(0.455)(-1) = 0.09\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(c)\n"
msgstr "(c)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Pauli | Ideal measurement outcome | Outcome after Pauli | Readout error | Undo Pauli | Final reported outcome | Probability |\n"
"|--------------|---------|----------|-------------|------------|------------|------------|\n"
"| I | 0 | 0 | None | I | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 99% = 24.75\\% |\n"
"| I | 0 | 0 | $0 \\rightarrow 1$ | I | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 1% = 0.25\\% |\n"
"| I | 1 | 1 | None | I | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 90% = 22.5\\% |\n"
"| I | 1 | 1 | $1 \\rightarrow 0$ | I | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 10% = 2.5\\% |\n"
"| X | 0 | 1 | None | X | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 90% = 22.5\\% |\n"
"| X | 0 | 1 | $1 \\rightarrow 0$ | X | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 10% = 2.5\\% |\n"
"| X | 1 | 0 | None | X | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 99% = 24.75\\% |\n"
"| X | 1 | 0 | $0 \\rightarrow 1$ | X | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 1% = 0.25\\% |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Pauli | Resultado ideal da medição | Resultado após Pauli | Erro de leitura | Desfazer Pauli | Resultado final relatado | Probabilidade |\n"
"|--------------|---------|----------|-------------|------------|------------|------------|\n"
"| I | 0 | 0 | Nenhum | I | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 99% = 24.75\\% |\n"
"| I | 0 | 0 | $0 \\rightarrow 1$ | I | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 1% = 0.25\\% |\n"
"| I | 1 | 1 | Nenhum | I | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 90% = 22.5\\% |\n"
"| I | 1 | 1 | $1 \\rightarrow 0$ | I | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 10% = 2.5\\% |\n"
"| X | 0 | 1 | Nenhum | X | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 90% = 22.5\\% |\n"
"| X | 0 | 1 | $1 \\rightarrow 0$ | X | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 10% = 2.5\\% |\n"
"| X | 1 | 0 | Nenhum | X | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 99% = 24.75\\% |\n"
"| X | 1 | 0 | $0 \\rightarrow 1$ | X | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 1% = 0.25\\% |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(d) From previous parts, we know the expectation values of Z in each of the final states. We need only take the weighted average:\n"
msgstr "(d) Das partes anteriores, conhecemos os valores esperados de Z em cada um dos estados finais. Só precisamos calcular a média ponderada:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle & = (0.2475)(1)+(0.0025)(-1)+(0.225)(-1)+(0.025)(1)\\\\\n"
"& + (0.225)(1)+(0.025)(-1)+(0.2475)(-1)+(0.0025)(1)\\\\\n"
"& = 0\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle & = (0.2475)(1)+(0.0025)(-1)+(0.225)(-1)+(0.025)(1)\\\\\n"
"& + (0.225)(1)+(0.025)(-1)+(0.2475)(-1)+(0.0025)(1)\\\\\n"
"& = 0\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(e) In this very simple case our application of twirling recovered exactly the ideal expectation value. That is not typical. What is typical is that the twirling undoes biases like those introduced through asymmetric transitions, and returns an expectation value closer to the ideal.\n"
msgstr "(e) Neste caso muito simples, nossa aplicação do twirling recuperou exatamente o valor esperado ideal. Isso não é típico. O que é típico é que o twirling desfaz vieses como os introduzidos por transições assimétricas e retorna um valor esperado mais próximo do ideal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(f) This is a toy model application. There could be several things missing. Notably, we have not run calibration circuits here to estimate a rescaling factor $a$. This is typically necessary.\n"
msgstr "(f) Esta é uma aplicação de modelo simplificado. Pode haver várias coisas faltando. Notavelmente, não executamos circuitos de calibração aqui para estimar um fator de reescalonamento $a$. Isso normalmente é necessário.\n"

