#, no-wrap
msgid "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"
msgstr "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the core idea behind PEC:\n"
msgstr "Esta é a ideia central do PEC:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample channels according to $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"
msgstr "Amostre canais de acordo com $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Attach signs to measurement outcomes\n"
msgstr "Atribua sinais aos resultados de medição\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expectation values converge to the noise-free value\n"
msgstr "Os valores esperados convergem para o valor sem ruído\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We apply PEC \"by hand\" to the estimation of $\\langle Z \\rangle$ by using the density matrix $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ and see if we can recover the results for $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. For $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$ we expect:\n"
msgstr "Aplicamos o PEC \"manualmente\" à estimativa de $\\langle Z \\rangle$ usando a matriz de densidade $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ e vemos se conseguimos recuperar os resultados de $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. Para $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$ esperamos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note also that for the noisy density matrix, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "Observe também que, para a matriz de densidade ruidosa, obtemos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It's the right order of magnitude but significantly far from the ideal case.\n"
msgstr "É a ordem de grandeza correta, mas significativamente distante do caso ideal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we step through how, with the PEC process, we can reconstruct the unbiased expectation value from the noisy density matrix. In real workflows, this is probabilistic and will be automated. In this \"by-hand\" workflow, we will choose probabilistic values that are realistic, but perhaps convenient for our presentation. This should not be taken as a claim that PEC is perfect. This is simply to show you a plausible scenario that could happen inside the PEC packages.\n"
msgstr "Agora vamos ver como, com o processo do PEC, podemos reconstruir o valor esperado sem viés a partir da matriz de densidade ruidosa. Em fluxos de trabalho reais, isso é probabilístico e será automatizado. Neste fluxo \"manual\", escolheremos valores probabilísticos realistas, mas talvez convenientes para a nossa apresentação. Isso não deve ser interpretado como uma afirmação de que o PEC é perfeito. É apenas para mostrar um cenário plausível que poderia acontecer dentro dos pacotes de PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that our noise channel is of the form:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"The inverse can be written (exactly):\n"
msgstr ""
"Lembre-se de que nosso canal de ruído tem a forma:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"O inverso pode ser escrito (exatamente) como:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is simpler for this introduction to focus on the channel's effect on our density matrix. This allows us to work with familiar objects like density matrices and expectation values. To that end, consider what must be true about the effects of this inverse operation on our estimation process: the estimator produced by PEC must be normalized and unbiased. This corresponds to two conditions:\n"
msgstr "Para esta introdução, é mais simples focar no efeito do canal sobre a nossa matriz de densidade. Isso nos permite trabalhar com objetos familiares, como matrizes de densidade e valores esperados. Para isso, considere o que deve ser verdade sobre os efeitos dessa operação inversa em nosso processo de estimativa: o estimador produzido pelo PEC deve ser normalizado e sem viés. Isso corresponde a duas condições:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normalization: To ensure that this operation does not change the scale of the observable, we require that $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. To see why this is the case, we could either consider the action of the inverse on a density matrix, or consider its action on the expectation value of something trivial like $\\mathcal{I}$ itself.\n"
msgstr "Normalização: para garantir que essa operação não altere a escala do observável, exigimos que $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. Para ver por que isso acontece, poderíamos considerar a ação do inverso sobre uma matriz de densidade, ou sua ação sobre o valor esperado de algo trivial como o próprio $\\mathcal{I}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calibration: In a real workflow, we use calibration circuits to learn noise behavior at a gate level. We then use the gate-level knowledge of noise behavior, and the linearity of expectation values to apply the learned noise model to the larger circuit. In our case, we started with artificial knowledge that the ideal expectation value $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. But it would be very easy to come up with a state for which we know theoretically that this would be the ideal value, and then use actual measurements for calibration. A key point is that for PEC, one typically does not learn a full noise model of the entire circuit. Instead, one learns local noise models for individual gates or circuit layers and uses those to construct the quasi-probability decomposition.\n"
msgstr "Calibração: em um fluxo de trabalho real, usamos circuitos de calibração para aprender o comportamento do ruído no nível das portas. Em seguida, usamos esse conhecimento do ruído no nível das portas, e a linearidade dos valores esperados, para aplicar o modelo de ruído aprendido ao circuito maior. No nosso caso, partimos do conhecimento artificial de que o valor esperado ideal é $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. Mas seria muito fácil criar um estado para o qual sabemos teoricamente que esse seria o valor ideal e depois usar medições reais para a calibração. Um ponto-chave é que, no PEC, normalmente não se aprende um modelo de ruído completo de todo o circuito. Em vez disso, aprendem-se modelos de ruído locais para portas individuais ou camadas do circuito e usam-se esses modelos para construir a decomposição em quase-probabilidades.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use these conditions to determine $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. We consider the ansatz\n"
msgstr "Usamos essas condições para determinar $\\alpha$ e $\\beta$. Consideramos o ansatz\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that the Pauli channels act by conjugation:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Lembre-se de que os canais de Pauli atuam por conjugação:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ to $\\rho$ gives:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Aplicar $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ a $\\rho$ resulta em:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Taking the trace, we obtain:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Tomando o traço, obtemos:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each Pauli operator is unitary, such that conjugation preserves the trace:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Cada operador de Pauli é unitário, de modo que a conjugação preserva o traço:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the PEC estimator to be normalized, the effective\n"
"inverse map must preserve the trace of all density matrices. That is, we require:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Para que o estimador do PEC seja normalizado, o mapa inverso efetivo\n"
"deve preservar o traço de todas as matrizes de densidade. Ou seja, exigimos:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies the normalization constraint:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Isso implica a restrição de normalização:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "But in our case, this yields the condition:\n"
msgstr "Mas, no nosso caso, isso gera a condição:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we use calibration information to relate the observed expectation value to the known ideal one.\n"
msgstr "Agora usamos as informações de calibração para relacionar o valor esperado observado ao valor ideal conhecido.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{ideal}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{ideal}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0.5\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"0.5\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Or equivalently,\n"
"$$\n"
"0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)=0.5\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Or equivalently,\n"
"$$\n"
"0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)=0.5\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solving our two conditions for $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "Resolvendo nossas duas condições para $\\alpha$ e $\\beta$, obtemos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"\\beta = -0.0625\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"\\beta = -0.0625\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These coefficients sum to 1, but one of them is negative.\n"
msgstr "Esses coeficientes somam 1, mas um deles é negativo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can recover the ideal expectation value by randomly modifying the circuit, measuring, multiplying the result by a signed weight, and averaging. In particular, no density matrices are reconstructed and no inverse channel is implemented physically.\n"
msgstr "Podemos recuperar o valor esperado ideal modificando o circuito aleatoriamente, medindo, multiplicando o resultado por um peso com sinal e calculando a média. Em particular, nenhuma matriz de densidade é reconstruída e nenhum canal inverso é implementado fisicamente.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The key step: this is PEC {#the-key-step-this-is-pec}"
msgstr "A etapa-chave: isto é o PEC {#the-key-step-this-is-pec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For our noise strength $p=0.15$, the inverse channel can be written as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1} =\\underbrace{1.1875}_{\\alpha}\\,\\mathcal{I}\n"
"\\;+\\;\n"
"\\underbrace{(-0.0625)}_{\\beta}\n"
"(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Para a nossa intensidade de ruído $p=0.15$, o canal inverso pode ser escrito como:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1} =\\underbrace{1.1875}_{\\alpha}\\,\\mathcal{I}\n"
"\\;+\\;\n"
"\\underbrace{(-0.0625)}_{\\beta}\n"
"(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Important facts:\n"
msgstr "Fatos importantes:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The coefficients sum to 1\n"
msgstr "Os coeficientes somam 1\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "One coefficient is negative\n"
msgstr "Um coeficiente é negativo\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each term is physically implementable\n"
msgstr "Cada termo é fisicamente implementável\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The negativity moves into classical post-processing\n"
msgstr "A negatividade é transferida para o pós-processamento clássico\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We form a sampling distribution from the absolute values of the weights:\n"
msgstr "Formamos uma distribuição de amostragem a partir dos valores absolutos dos pesos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\alpha| = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"|\\beta| = 0.0625\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\alpha| = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"|\\beta| = 0.0625\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(for each of X, Y, Z)\n"
msgstr "(para cada um de X, Y, Z)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Total weight:\n"
"$$\n"
"W = 1.1875 + 3\\times0.0625 = 1.375\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Peso total:\n"
"$$\n"
"W = 1.1875 + 3\\times0.0625 = 1.375\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For sampling probabilities, divide by W.\n"
msgstr "Para obter as probabilidades de amostragem, divida por W.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Operation | Probability | Sign |\n"
"|-----------|-------------|------|\n"
"| Do nothing ($\\mathcal{I}$) |1.1875 / 1.375 ≈ 0.864 |+ |\n"
"| Apply X | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Apply Y | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Apply Z | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Operação | Probabilidade | Sinal |\n"
"|-----------|-------------|------|\n"
"| Não fazer nada ($\\mathcal{I}$) |1.1875 / 1.375 ≈ 0.864 |+ |\n"
"| Aplicar X | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Aplicar Y | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Aplicar Z | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sign comes from the original coefficient, not the probability.\n"
msgstr "O sinal vem do coeficiente original, não da probabilidade.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each shot consists of these steps:\n"
msgstr "Cada shot consiste nestas etapas:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the state\n"
msgstr "Preparar o estado\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let the hardware apply the noisy circuit\n"
msgstr "Deixar o hardware aplicar o circuito ruidoso\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Randomly choose an operation from the table above using the associated probabilities\n"
msgstr "Escolher aleatoriamente uma operação da tabela acima usando as probabilidades associadas\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply it\n"
msgstr "Apply it\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure $Z$, getting $\\pm 1$\n"
msgstr "Medir $Z$, obtendo $\\pm 1$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiply the outcome by $\\text{sign} \\times W$\n"
msgstr "Multiplicar o resultado por $\\text{sign} \\times W$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Record that number\n"
msgstr "Registrar esse número\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now do examples of several shots.\n"
msgstr "Agora vamos ver exemplos de vários shots.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Shot 1 (identity case)**\n"
msgstr "**Shot 1 (caso da identidade)**\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose our randomly chosen operation is the identity $\\mathcal{I}$ (or equivalently: do nothing). Based on the arguments and the table above, this will happen 86.4% of the time. Because the coefficient of $\\mathcal{I}$ in the inverse of the noise channel is positive, we select the $+$ sign. Our measurement of Z could easily yield either $\\pm 1$. Let us suppose it yields $+1$.\n"
msgstr "Suponha que a operação escolhida aleatoriamente seja a identidade $\\mathcal{I}$ (ou, de forma equivalente: não fazer nada). Com base nos argumentos e na tabela acima, isso acontecerá em 86,4% das vezes. Como o coeficiente de $\\mathcal{I}$ no inverso do canal de ruído é positivo, selecionamos o sinal $+$. Nossa medição de Z poderia facilmente resultar em $\\pm 1$. Vamos supor que resulte em $+1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The PEC-corrected contribution from this shot would be:\n"
"$(+1) \\times (+1) \\times 1.375 = +1.375$\n"
msgstr ""
"A contribuição corrigida pelo PEC deste shot seria:\n"
"$(+1) \\times (+1) \\times 1.375 = +1.375$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Shot 2 (identity again)**\n"
msgstr "**Shot 2 (identidade novamente)**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose we again obtain $\\mathcal{I}$ as our random operation (so the sign of the term is initially still $+$), but this time our measurement of Z yields $-1$. This time the contribution is:\n"
"$$\n"
"(-1) \\times (+1) \\times 1.375 = -1.375\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Suponha que obtenhamos novamente $\\mathcal{I}$ como operação aleatória (portanto o sinal do termo ainda é inicialmente $+$), mas desta vez nossa medição de Z resulta em $-1$. Desta vez a contribuição é:\n"
"$$\n"
"(-1) \\times (+1) \\times 1.375 = -1.375\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Shot 3 (X chosen)**\n"
msgstr "**Shot 3 (X escolhido)**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This time our random operation is X. This term in the inverse is negative, so we keep a $-$ sign. We apply X and then measure Z. Again, we could obtain either eigenvalue; say we obtain $-1$. The contribution from this term is:\n"
msgstr "Desta vez nossa operação aleatória é X. Este termo no inverso é negativo, então mantemos o sinal $-$. Aplicamos X e depois medimos Z. Novamente, poderíamos obter qualquer um dos autovalores; digamos que obtemos $-1$. A contribuição deste termo é:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(-1) \\times (-1) \\times 1.375 = +1.375\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(-1) \\times (-1) \\times 1.375 = +1.375\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Shot 4 (Z chosen)**\n"
msgstr "**Shot 4 (Z escolhido)**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The random operation is Z. This gives us a $-$ sign from the table. Suppose we measure Z and obtain $+1$. The contribution is:\n"
msgstr "A operação aleatória é Z. Isso nos dá o sinal $-$ da tabela. Suponha que medimos Z e obtemos $+1$. A contribuição é:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(+1) \\times (-1) \\times 1.375 = -1.375\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(+1) \\times (-1) \\times 1.375 = -1.375\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Shot 5 (Y chosen)**\n"
msgstr "**Shot 5 (Y escolhido)**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The random operation is Y. This gives us a $-$ sign from the table. Suppose we measure Z and obtain $+1$. The contribution is:\n"
msgstr "A operação aleatória é Y. Isso nos dá o sinal $-$ da tabela. Suponha que medimos Z e obtemos $+1$. A contribuição é:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Averaging the results**\n"
msgstr "**Calculando a média dos resultados**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Imagine we collect many such PEC-weighted outcomes:\n"
msgstr "Imagine que coletamos muitos desses resultados ponderados pelo PEC:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{ +1.375,-1.375,+1.375,-1.375,-1.375,\\dots \\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{ +1.375,-1.375,+1.375,-1.375,-1.375,\\dots \\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By construction, we apply the identity 86.4% of the time. We apply each of the other gates 4.5% of the time. In a real workflow, we don't know the precise underlying states, nor the entire noise channel. But we do know the weighting factor $W \\equiv 1.375$ from above, and the relative probability with which we apply each operation. In a real workflow, we rely on the unknown density matrix to give us measurement outcomes. We will verify here that this procedure would yield the correct results.\n"
msgstr "Por construção, aplicamos a identidade em 86,4% das vezes. Aplicamos cada uma das outras portas em 4,5% das vezes. Em um fluxo de trabalho real, não conhecemos os estados subjacentes precisos, nem todo o canal de ruído. Mas conhecemos o fator de ponderação $W \\equiv 1.375$ acima e a probabilidade relativa com que aplicamos cada operação. Em um fluxo de trabalho real, contamos com a matriz de densidade desconhecida para nos fornecer os resultados das medições. Verificaremos aqui que esse procedimento produziria os resultados corretos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We want to calculate the average of all weighted, signed measurements including applications of Pauli operators $P_i$ prior to measurement. Call the total number of all shots $N_\\text{shots}$. Call the set of all shots for which Pauli $P_i$ was applied $S_{P_i}$ and use $j$ to index these shots. Call the measurement outcome of the $j^\\text{th}$ shot under the application of the $i^\\text{th}$ Pauli $z_{ij}$. We can write this average as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC} = \\frac{W}{N_\\text{shots}}\\sum_{i\\in \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}} \\text{sign}_i \\sum_{j\\in S_{P_i}}{ z_{i,j}}\n"
"$$\n"
"The Pauli operator $P_i$ is applied probabilistically with probability $p_i$. In the limit of a large number of shots,\n"
"$$\n"
"p_i = \\frac{\\text{Number of shots with Pauli } P_i \\text{ applied}}{N_\\text{shots}}\n"
"$$\n"
"We can use this to write:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\frac{1}{N_\\text{shots}}\\sum_{j\\in S_{P_i}}{z_{i,j}} & = \\frac{p_i}{N_{\\text{shots with }P_i}}\\sum_{j\\in S_{P_i}}{ z_{i,j}}\\\\\n"
"&  = p_i \\langle Z \\rangle_{P_i}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $\\langle Z \\rangle_{P_i}$ is the expectation value of Z only over the ensemble of shots in which $P_i$ was applied. This is useful because we know what each such expectation value must be from the density matrix. Again, in a real workflow, this would emerge from measurement, not from a known density matrix.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{I} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZI\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}I\\right) = 0.4\\\\\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{X} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZX\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}X\\right) = -0.4\\\\\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{Y} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZY\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}Y\\right) = -0.4\\\\\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{Z} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZZ\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}Z\\right) = 0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Queremos calcular a média de todas as medições ponderadas e com sinal, incluindo as aplicações de operadores de Pauli $P_i$ antes da medição. Chame o número total de shots de $N_\\text{shots}$. Chame o conjunto de todos os shots para os quais o Pauli $P_i$ foi aplicado de $S_{P_i}$ e use $j$ para indexar esses shots. Chame o resultado da medição do $j^\\text{th}$ shot sob a aplicação do $i^\\text{th}$ Pauli de $z_{ij}$. Podemos escrever essa média como:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC} = \\frac{W}{N_\\text{shots}}\\sum_{i\\in \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}} \\text{sign}_i \\sum_{j\\in S_{P_i}}{ z_{i,j}}\n"
"$$\n"
"O operador de Pauli $P_i$ é aplicado probabilisticamente com probabilidade $p_i$. No limite de um grande número de shots,\n"
"$$\n"
"p_i = \\frac{\\text{Number of shots with Pauli } P_i \\text{ applied}}{N_\\text{shots}}\n"
"$$\n"
"Podemos usar isso para escrever:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\frac{1}{N_\\text{shots}}\\sum_{j\\in S_{P_i}}{z_{i,j}} & = \\frac{p_i}{N_{\\text{shots with }P_i}}\\sum_{j\\in S_{P_i}}{ z_{i,j}}\\\\\n"
"&  = p_i \\langle Z \\rangle_{P_i}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"onde $\\langle Z \\rangle_{P_i}$ é o valor esperado de Z apenas sobre o conjunto de shots em que $P_i$ foi aplicado. Isso é útil porque sabemos qual deve ser cada um desses valores esperados a partir da matriz de densidade. Novamente, em um fluxo de trabalho real, isso surgiria da medição, não de uma matriz de densidade conhecida.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{I} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZI\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}I\\right) = 0.4\\\\\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{X} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZX\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}X\\right) = -0.4\\\\\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{Y} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZY\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}Y\\right) = -0.4\\\\\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{Z} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZZ\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}Z\\right) = 0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

